2026-11-01T01:26:20.0738638Z -- Building presets (item 17)
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739043Z   ok   a masonry house has more thermal mass than a timber one
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739177Z   ok   an older house loses more heat
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739298Z   ok   loss scales with heated area
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739457Z   ok   floor heating adds an actively charged store
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739618Z   ok   radiators respond faster than floor heating
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0739850Z   ok   timber-on-slab over a crawl space is the crawl-space house, exactly
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0740173Z   ok   the subtraction only fires under a crawl-space foundation
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0740427Z   ok   masonry over a crawl space keeps its walls -- nothing was removed twice
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0740667Z   ok   a concrete slab over a crawl space loses the slab but keeps the concrete
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0740816Z   ok   a heated basement adds both mass and loss
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0740999Z   ok   the heavy mass lives in the heated slab, and only there
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0741163Z   ok   the radiator power fraction follows the emitters
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0741351Z   ok   a radiator loop is a small store, not the building's slab
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0741597Z   ok   radiators can deliver the design heat load at a sane flow temperature
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0741810Z   ok   with radiators the heavy floor coasts as part of the room store
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0742110Z   ok   nonsense options are clamped rather than propagated
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0742363Z   ok   a valid non-radiator emitter is kept, only an unknown one is clamped
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0742532Z   ok   derived values are accepted by the thermal model
2026-11-01T01:26:20.0742539Z 
